WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.233
Out of

00:00:00.233 --> 00:00:01.801
two music music legends

00:00:01.801 --> 00:00:04.037
who knew and worked with Tina Turner.

00:00:04.037 --> 00:00:04.704
Grammy Award

00:00:04.704 --> 00:00:05.705
winner Ruth Pointer,

00:00:05.705 --> 00:00:06.573
the last surviving member

00:00:06.573 --> 00:00:07.107
of the Pointer

00:00:07.107 --> 00:00:08.008
Sisters, whose

00:00:08.008 --> 00:00:09.342
first album, I should say, Ruth

00:00:09.342 --> 00:00:11.111
turns 50 this month.

00:00:11.111 --> 00:00:11.745
I know

00:00:11.745 --> 00:00:13.346
that is something on a sad day, though,

00:00:13.346 --> 00:00:14.180
to think about it.

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:15.315
Incredible

00:00:15.382 --> 00:00:16.516
to celebrate

00:00:16.516 --> 00:00:17.050
your many hits

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:17.450
include I'm

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:18.151
So Excited

00:00:18.151 --> 00:00:20.053
and Jump and Grammy Award winner

00:00:20.053 --> 00:00:20.820
Bryan Adams

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:21.321
whose songs

00:00:21.321 --> 00:00:23.223
you all know include everything I Do.

00:00:23.223 --> 00:00:25.892
I do it for you and Run to you.

00:00:25.892 --> 00:00:27.861
I am so grateful to have both of you

00:00:27.861 --> 00:00:29.129
on to talk about

00:00:29.129 --> 00:00:29.529
a woman

00:00:29.529 --> 00:00:30.397
that you admired,

00:00:30.397 --> 00:00:31.398
that you performed with,

00:00:31.398 --> 00:00:33.033
who you consider a friend.

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:33.900
Ruth,

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:35.935
what did you first think when you heard

00:00:36.202 --> 00:00:38.371
that Tina Turner had passed away today?

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:41.241
Oh, my God.

00:00:41.241 --> 00:00:42.876
I just started weeping.

00:00:42.876 --> 00:00:44.144
You know,

00:00:45.278 --> 00:00:47.614
I, I loved her so much.

00:00:47.781 --> 00:00:48.615
In my opinion,

00:00:48.615 --> 00:00:50.850
she was my queen in the music industry.

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:52.352
She was my queen.

00:00:52.352 --> 00:00:53.820
I wanted to be her.

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:54.287
You know,

00:00:54.287 --> 00:00:59.359
I tried to be her with my sisters and I.

00:00:59.426 --> 00:01:00.827
I saw her several times.

00:01:00.827 --> 00:01:03.163
I actually saw her with Ike in Oakland

00:01:03.163 --> 00:01:04.898
right after I graduated high school

00:01:04.898 --> 00:01:07.467
at a little juke joint there in Oakland.

00:01:07.801 --> 00:01:08.868
Sportsman's Club.

00:01:08.868 --> 00:01:11.337
We used to go to with the cats, and

00:01:12.272 --> 00:01:14.340
I was never the same after that.

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:15.842
But I've seen her concerts

00:01:15.842 --> 00:01:18.511
and I saw her musical and

00:01:18.511 --> 00:01:20.713
and we did The World Together, and

00:01:21.781 --> 00:01:24.551
she's watched us perform at clubs.

00:01:24.584 --> 00:01:25.485
I remember once her

00:01:25.485 --> 00:01:27.087
standing up side of the stage,

00:01:27.087 --> 00:01:29.355
we didn't even know she was there. Wow.

00:01:29.355 --> 00:01:31.157
And they came and told us

00:01:31.157 --> 00:01:32.125
that you've got a guest

00:01:32.125 --> 00:01:33.493
that's watching you perform.

00:01:33.493 --> 00:01:36.062
And we can say again, it was Tina.

00:01:36.062 --> 00:01:37.564
And we just fell apart

00:01:37.564 --> 00:01:38.565
and she said,

00:01:38.565 --> 00:01:40.500
you guys look like for Tina.

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:42.135
Turner is up there on that stage

00:01:42.135 --> 00:01:43.603
because we were tearing it up.

00:01:44.671 --> 00:01:45.905
I can only imagine what that

00:01:45.905 --> 00:01:47.040
moment must have been like.

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:47.774
I mean,

00:01:47.941 --> 00:01:49.843
you know, you both worked with her

00:01:49.843 --> 00:01:50.777
and perform with her.

00:01:50.777 --> 00:01:53.012
Brian, you recorded a duet with her,

00:01:53.012 --> 00:01:54.347
It's Only Love

00:01:54.347 --> 00:01:56.683
and that was released in 1985.

00:01:56.983 --> 00:01:58.485
You know, a lot of people have seen this,

00:01:58.485 --> 00:02:00.820
but I just want to play it

00:02:04.557 --> 00:02:05.258
and

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:10.830
I don't know.

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:12.899
And you worked together again, Brian,

00:02:12.899 --> 00:02:14.200
when you wrote the song back

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:15.068
where you started

00:02:15.068 --> 00:02:16.803
and you wrote that for her.

00:02:16.803 --> 00:02:19.339
Here's here's part of that

00:02:28.648 --> 00:02:29.616
And that song

00:02:29.616 --> 00:02:30.116
she won

00:02:30.116 --> 00:02:31.718
a Grammy in 1987

00:02:31.718 --> 00:02:35.088
for best female rock vocal performance.

00:02:35.388 --> 00:02:36.923
What memories can you share

00:02:36.923 --> 00:02:39.325
Brian of working with her.

00:02:39.325 --> 00:02:41.794
Well my god yeah right.

00:02:42.662 --> 00:02:43.096
I'm

00:02:44.531 --> 00:02:47.300
incredibly sad I've been all day today

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:48.635
since I read the news and

00:02:49.636 --> 00:02:50.503
it's it's taken

00:02:50.503 --> 00:02:52.005
a lot to actually even do this

00:02:52.005 --> 00:02:53.339
interview because,

00:02:53.339 --> 00:02:53.673
you know,

00:02:53.673 --> 00:02:55.175
she was not only

00:02:55.175 --> 00:02:57.710
really kind to me in the beginning, but

00:02:59.846 --> 00:03:01.714
just fabulous to work for.

00:03:01.714 --> 00:03:04.651
And I I'll tell you one story

00:03:04.651 --> 00:03:05.084
which probably

00:03:05.084 --> 00:03:05.785
nobody knows,

00:03:05.785 --> 00:03:06.786
which is the story

00:03:06.786 --> 00:03:07.921
when I recorded back

00:03:07.921 --> 00:03:09.389
when you started with her

00:03:09.389 --> 00:03:11.524
and she came into the studio and

00:03:12.926 --> 00:03:14.727
we ran the song down quickly.

00:03:14.727 --> 00:03:15.361
And I just

00:03:15.361 --> 00:03:16.963
when I started talking to the engineer

00:03:16.963 --> 00:03:17.397
and I said,

00:03:17.397 --> 00:03:18.331
okay, listen,

00:03:18.331 --> 00:03:19.432
